### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat to Validity | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Thermal Throttling** | CPU/GPU heat profiles differ; sustained runs may slow the CPU more than the GPU. | Record clock speeds and temperatures during all runs; report "Clock-Gated" vs "Sustained" speeds. |
| **Kernel Overhead** | Vulkan/CUDA launch overheads may differ significantly from CPU overheads for small batches. | Use a fixed batch size (e.g., 1) and report "Time to First Token" separately from "Steady State" speed. |
| **Quantization Disparity** | If different bit-depths are used to fit the model into different backends. | **Control:** Ensure all backends use the exact same weight quantization (e.g., GGUF Q4_K_M). |
| **Non-Deterministic Output** | Variations in floating-point math across backends may produce different text. | **Control:** Use a fixed seed and a "Fixed Prompt" test; report the exact string output to verify parity. |

